== Trivia ==
<!--
Die is the singular form of the word dice. Please do not change the word die to dice.
-->

* A spindown die is a type of die used as a life counter for ''Magic: The Gathering'' or for various other uses across card and board games. It is a D20 with the numbers laid out in a sequential pattern, to allow for the face-up number to be changed easily when a player's life goes up or down.
* The item's color scheme matches the D8 die included in ''The Binding of Isaac: Four Souls'' card game, which is used as a spindown die to keep track of an enemy's health.
* Spindown Dice is the only dice item that cannot be copied by the {{I|D infinity}}.
** It is arguable that Spindown Dice is not necessarily a dice item, since its effect does not involve random generation.
* Spindown Dice itself will be rerolled into {{I|Anima Sola}}, while {{I|Hypercoagulation}} rerolls into it.
* Using Spindown Dice on {{I|Smart Fly}} rerolls into {{I|Clear Rune}}, which is the only ''Repentance'' added item to reroll from a ''Rebirth'' one. This is due to the item taking up a previously unused item id.
* Two items are impossible to obtain with Spindown Dice:
** {{i|Mom's Ring}}, as it has the highest ID of all items (without mods taking a higher number, etc).
** {{I|Strawman}}, due to {{I|Dad's Note}} having immunity to being rerolled.
*** Even with {{I|Car Battery}}, {{I|Sausage}} will still spin down into {{I|Dad's Note}}
* Defeating {{E|Delirium}} as most tainted characters will unlock an item that is similar to their gameplay characteristic. However, Tainted Isaac's passive ability to have multiple items cycle on an item pedestal ({{I|Glitched Crown}}) is unlocked through defeating {{E|The Beast}} instead.

